- Ask for copies of any ordered tests and a clear plan for follow-up and referrals.

When to go directly to cardiology or ER
- ER immediately: extremely high BP with symptoms (see top), acute chest pain, stroke symptoms again, sudden severe shortness of breath, loss of consciousness.
- Cardiology referral urgently: persistent uncontrolled BP despite meds, new cardiac symptoms, documented arrhythmia, abnormal EKG or echo suggesting structural heart disease.

