  - Symptoms of heart disease (chest pain, shortness of breath, palpitations, syncope)
  - Abnormal ECG, heart murmurs, or suspected heart failure
  - Need for more advanced testing (echocardiogram, stress test, ambulatory BP monitoring, rhythm monitoring)
  - Secondary prevention planning after stroke (cardiology input for vascular risk management)
